      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: I believe this to still be the case. It's a common place and well known issue especially for stations on avatars, where people attempting to sit in the station will come out mangled and with their viewpoint significantly out of position. A line you'll often hear spoken is, \"Oh hang on, let me try and hold the seat more upright, try again now.\"\n\nThis applies to things like vehicles too, where in my Safari world we warn people not to park the car on a slope, or else it can be difficult to take control of it again. More advanced worlds use additional scripts such as that developed by Sacchan to resolve this, with worlds such as Test Pilots blowing many creators mind when it first released, amazed to see stations that actually worked so reliably. These scripts also aren't possible to use on avatars.\n\nOther issues include the station component not having any built in way to correctly seat avatars at a hip to seat basis, or to adjust seated height by viewpoint to a desired location. (A function that Sacchans script also provides)\n\nThese would be highly desirable features to include, if any work is being done to stations.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
