      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You can better work around this issue by setting the station rotation to Quaternion.Identity, then call .UseAttachedStation(), then in OnStationEntered you set the station back to the original/desired rotation.\n\nI'm doing this in my \"Auto-Calibration Chair Script\" asset since a few years and it works flawless.\n\nThe workaround that was posted above probably only works as long as the localRotation at start happens to be Quaternion.Identity so I wouldn't recommend it as a general solution for everyone.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-06-29T05:02:01.615Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When sitting on a station in VR, the higher the world space X or Z rotation of the station's seat object, the more offset your seated position will be, making rotated chairs basically unusable. This is a particular problem for vehicles which may be parked on a slope.\nThe rotation of the chair only matters when you enter it. Once you are on a chair it can rotate any amount and your offset from it will not change.\nI have created a test world with 2 pickupable chairs, one is the standard VRCChair, and the other is a VRCChair with a custom udonsharp script to fix the problem.\nwrld_3220b9ec-965b-4573-bacc-e4341e2fca1a\nTry rotating each chair to different angles and noticing the offset.\nThe code for the workaround is:\npublic class VRCChair3_Fix : UdonSharpBehaviour\n{\n    private Transform Seat;\n    private Quaternion SeatStartRot;\n    VRCPlayerApi localPlayer;\n    void Start()\n    {\n        localPlayer = Networking.LocalPlayer;\n        Seat = ((VRC.SDK3.Components.VRCStation)GetComponent(typeof(VRC.SDK3.Components.VRCStation))).stationEnterPlayerLocation.transform;\n        SeatStartRot = Seat.localRotation;\n    }\n    private void Interact()\n    {\n        Seat.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(0, Seat.eulerAngles.y, 0);//fixes offset seated position when getting in a rolled/pitched vehicle\n        localPlayer.UseAttachedStation();\n        Seat.localRotation = SeatStartRot;\n    }\n}\nThis is a hack to fix the problem, but it works perfectly. Either this should be done internally in VRChat, or the math that breaks when entering a slanted seat should be fixed.\nDesktop mode does not have this problem.",
